<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narmadapuram district</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hoshangabad district</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narmadapuram district, known as Hoshangabad district until 2022, is a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> river. Its headquarters, the town of Hoshangabad (now Narmadapuram), was named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoshang-shah">Hoshang Shah</a> of the Malwa Sultanate. The district contains the hill station of Pachmarhi and the Satpura Tiger Reserve.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narmadapuram-district.jpg" alt="Narmadapuram district" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M Starlord · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chauragarh,_Pachmarhi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
